I will help you create a PayPal order and verify it on your server. Based on your needs, we should first determine if you want to test in the Sandbox or Production environment.

### 1. Create an Order
Using the PayPal REST API, here is the server-side pattern for creating an order (assuming USD currency). Replace the base URL with `api-m.sandbox.paypal.com` or `api-m.paypal.com` based on your environment:

```javascript
const createOrder = async (amount, currency = 'USD') => {
  const token = await getToken();
  const res = await fetch('https://api-m.paypal.com/v2/checkout/orders', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'Authorization': `Bearer ${token}`,
      'Content-Type': 'application/json'
    },
    body: JSON.stringify({
      intent: 'CAPTURE',
      purchase_units: [{
        amount: { currency_code: currency, value: amount.toFixed(2) },
        custom_id: 'your-internal-order-id'
      }]
    })
  });
  return res.json();
};
```

### 2. Verify the Order
Before you fulfill the order or capture payment, you must strictly validate the order details on your server to prevent tampering by the client:

```javascript
const order = await fetch(`https://api-m.paypal.com/v2/checkout/orders/${orderId}`, {
  headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${token}` }
}).then(r => r.json());

if (order.status !== 'APPROVED') throw new Error('Not approved');
if (order.purchase_units[0].amount.value !== expectedAmount) throw new Error('Amount mismatch');
if (order.purchase_units[0].amount.currency_code !== expectedCurrency) throw new Error('Currency mismatch');
if (order.purchase_units[0].payee.merchant_id !== YOUR_MERCHANT_ID) throw new Error('Wrong merchant');
```
After verifying these fields, you can securely proceed to capture the payment.
